  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"line-height: 1.6em; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 200; color: #fafafa;\">🚀 <strong>Frontend</strong> Focus</td></tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #fafafa;\"><p>#​768 — November 25, 2026 | <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193427/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #fafafa; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the web</a></p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193386/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1795606329/zfisuejumjtruxporeby.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193386/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Things You Can Do With a Browser in 2027</a></span> — Luigi returns with a sequel to the popular <em><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193387/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">browser-2020</a></em> list, highlighting some of the lesser-known things browsers can do today, including HTML-in-Canvas, the &lt;<code>model</code>&gt; element, HDR, on-device AI, hardware APIs, and more. Each feature is quickly explained alongside a browser support table.</p>\n<p>Luigi De Rosa </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193385/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/e6eb34ef.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193385/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.meticulous.ai\">Agents Didn’t Clear Your Plate. They Dumped Reviews on It</a></span> — Your agents write PRs in minutes, then eat your afternoon in review. When did ‘saving time’ start to mean babysitting agents’ work? Meticulous verifies every UI change, with no developer effort. Devs at Dropbox &amp; ElevenLabs have their afternoons back. You can too.</p>\n<p>Meticulous <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193388/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"lea.verou.me\">Nudeps: npm Imports in the Browser</a></span> — A new tool from Lea Verou and Dmitry Sharabin that lets you <code>npm install</code> packages and import them by name directly within the browser, <em>no bundler required</em>. It builds upon thinking outlined in Lea's '<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193389/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Web dependencies are broken</a>' article from earlier this year.</p>\n<p>Lea Verou </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193390/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"css-tricks.com\">When Everything Has Changed, What Do We Do Next?</a></span> — A post that takes stock of the year we've had, where the AI bubble has undoubtedly reshaped the industry. Andy argues that developers are more than \"code slingers,\" and makes the case for investing in people, building by hand, and keeping independent publishing alive.</p>\n<p>Andy Bell </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">⚡️</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;\">IN BRIEF</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🦊 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193394/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Firefox 161 is out</a> and adds support for the CSS <code>random()</code> function (more on that later), plus <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193395/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Compression Dictionary Transport</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🐞 The Ladybird browser (an effort to build a new browser engine <em>from scratch</em>) is <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193391/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">now in alpha</a>, available for macOS and Linux. You can <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193392/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">download it here</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>⚙️ Simon Willison has been trying the above Ladybird alpha and <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193393/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">shares his initial thoughts here</a>, calling it an \"<em>astonishingly ambitious project</em>\".</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">📙</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">Articles, Opinions &amp; Tutorials</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193398/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.mozilla.org\">Why There Are Still No Non-WebKit Browsers on iOS</a></span> — Mozilla says that, three years on, the EU's DMA (along with Japan's newer rules) has ultimately failed to open up iOS to any non-WebKit browser engines.</p>\n<p>Mozilla </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 After an open letter from Mozilla, Shopify and others, the European Commission <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193399/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">says it's in talks with Apple</a>, and <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193400/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome's team has backed Mozilla's stance</a> too.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193401/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"piccalil.li\">Understanding CSS <code>random()</code></a></span> — As mentioned above, Firefox 161 has joined Chrome and Safari in supporting <code>random()</code>. Here, Mat uses it to give his sidenotes a hand-placed 'jauntiness'.</p>\n<p>Mat Marquis </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193402/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"developer-api.foxit.com\">Foxit Compares 10 HTML to PDF APIs</a></span> — Rendering engines, CSS and JavaScript handling, headers and footers, and how each API bills a render.</p>\n<p>Foxit <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193403/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1795605137/msdmg5nudeckjanlck1b.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"230\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193403/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.iron-out.io\">Has the Web Stopped Getting Heavier?</a></span> — The pace at which web pages get heavier is levelling off, as HTTP Archive data shows growth has slowed to a crawl, with the median mobile page adding just 7KB of JavaScript in the past year.</p>\n<p>Sander van Surksum </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193404/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1795607611/lhjnqjomhx3egtbrjt4r.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193404/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"css-tricks.com\">Beyond 12 Columns: Designing Layouts With Personality</a></span> — CSS Grid really changed what was possible for page layouts, but Andy notes that designers still lean heavily on the twelve-column pattern. So he explores some more ambitious layout options that can be easily achieved today.</p>\n<p>Andy Clarke </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193405/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"kittygiraudel.com\">Playing with CSS Layers</a></span> — A fun tinkering post from Kitty, experimenting with CSS layers on their personal site just for the joy of it.</p>\n<p>Kitty Giraudel </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193406/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.master.dev\">The Compacting Sidebar Blues</a></span> — What should an app's sidebar do on a screen that's too short for it? Chris explains why a <code>scroll-state()</code> query loops infinitely here, and what works better instead.</p>\n<p>Chris Coyier </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193407/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">AI Sped Up The Build: How Can Accessibility Testing Keep Up?</a></span>\n<br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Andrew Chung</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193408/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">A New Set of HTML Insertion and Streaming APIs</a></span>\n<br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Amit Merchant</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193409/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Creating Diagrams and Graphs Using Modern CSS</a></span>\n<br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Temani Afif</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">🧰</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">Tools, Code &amp; Resources</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193410/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1795540051/hhyexxoynzowzrgr0kac.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193410/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"buttons.joshwcomeau.com\">Button Sounds: Tactile SFX for Your UI</a></span> — Josh has pulled together a free collection of 50+ professionally recorded multi-sampled clicks and toggles. Many have the charming thunks and clunks of your favorite keyboard. Distributed as <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193411/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">an NPM package</a> with optional React bindings.</p>\n<p>Josh W. Comeau </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193412/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.tigerdata.com\">Your Chart Isn’t Slow. Its Query Is</a></span> — TimescaleDB extends Postgres so dashboards stay fast as data grows. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193412/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">$1000 credit on Tiger Cloud</a>.</p>\n<p>Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193413/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"alloyhtml.com\">Alloy CSS: One Stylesheet for the HTML Your Server Renders</a></span> — A free kit of dialogs, menus, drawers, tabs and toast notifications that all work with JavaScript turned off.</p>\n<p>Fandy Pradana </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>🤖</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193414/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">wllama 4.0: Run llama.cpp Models in the Browser</a></span> — These WebAssembly bindings for llama.cpp let you run GGUF models directly in-browser. v4 doubles inference speed, and models of any size now load, with WebGPU helping out (where available). <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193415/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Try the demos here.</a></p>\n<p>Xuan-Son Nguyen </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>⏱️</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193416/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\"><code>&lt;relative-time&gt;</code> 5.5: Format Timestamps as a Localized Relative Time</a></span> — Supply this web component with a standard date/time and it'll render <em>\"2 days ago\"</em>, say. GitHub uses this on its repo and code views.</p>\n<p>GitHub </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193417/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.bram.us\">'CodePen Commander' Brings Pens into Your Local Editor</a></span> — If you use CodePen Pro, Bramus has built a CLI tool that brings <code>git</code>-style clone/push workflows to CodePen 2.0, along with batch syncing, a local dev server, and one-command deploys.</p>\n<p>Bramus Van Damme </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193418/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"introjs.com\">Intro.js: A User-Friendly 'Onboarding Tour' Library</a></span> — A library for creating step-by-step product tours (as seen during onboarding in SaaS tools, for example). It's AGPL licensed with an optional paid license available too.</p>\n<p>Afshin Mehrabani </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193419/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Port Menu: A Tiny macOS Menu Bar App To Track Dev Servers Across Projects</a></span>\n<br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Eduard Wieandt</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>⚡ AI agents ignore rules. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/193420/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Nexity’s reviewer agents check every new Next.js + Sanity section</a> against yours: design, schema, GROQ.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">🕹️</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">...and finally</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpa